oXiDe SE syscall interface exception
====================================

Project: oXiDe SE
Applies to: this repository only

This file states an additional permission granted by the copyright
holders of this repository for their respective contributions.

Additional permission
---------------------

In addition to the rights granted by CeCILL v2.1, the copyright holders
of this repository permit the creation, execution and distribution of
software that communicates with this code base solely through the public
system call interface exposed by the running platform, without causing
that separate software to become subject to CeCILL v2.1 solely because
of that communication.

Conditions
----------

This exception applies only if all of the following are true:

- the separate software does not modify this repository's code base;
- the separate software does not incorporate or link code from this
  repository, except by invoking the public system call interface of the
  running platform;
- the interaction with this repository is limited to the public system
  calls exposed by the platform.

Effect on modifications
-----------------------

Any modification of this repository itself remains governed by CeCILL
v2.1. This exception does not change the licensing obligations that
apply to changes made to the code base contained in this repository.

Project intent
--------------

This exception is intended to clarify, in a manner similar in spirit to
the syscall boundary used by operating system kernels such as Linux,
that applications and other software may run on top of the platform and
use its public system calls without having to be CeCILL-compatible for
that reason alone.

This repository is an open source implementation proposal around public
GlobalPlatform specifications. It is provided without any claim of
exhaustiveness, certification or industrial conformance.

